## Memory Protocol

1. **Read `MEMORY.md` at session start.** It is the always-loaded index.
2. **`MEMORY.md` is an index, not a store** (~150-line ceiling). It points to `memory/*.md` files, each one topic, loaded only when relevant.
3. **Memory file types:** `user_*` (who they are), `feedback_*` (how to work with them), `reference_*` (facts, ids, configs), `project_*` (ongoing work). Frontmatter on every file: `name`, `description`, `type`.
4. **Split rule:** prescriptive always/never rules live in THIS file. Facts that change live in `memory/`. Never duplicate a rule across files.
5. **Session audit on wrap-up:** scan for corrections, new facts, implied rules. File them silently. Dedupe on write.
6. **Archive past the ceiling.** Move stale entries to `00_System/archive.md`. Never delete a working rule.

